Theorem DP-9: cow_mode 5-row classification with row (c) joint DP-5 refinement

  Preconditions:
    - s is a canonical AimsState per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
    - cow_mode :
        AimsState x ArcVarId x FieldPath x ProgramPoint -> CowMode
      per Annex E §AIMS DP-9 + Appendix C truth table
    - CowMode is the closed sum type
        CowMode = StaticUnique | StaticShared | Dynamic
      per aims-proof/proofs/01-decisions/Decision.proof lines 58-59
    - DP-9 is context-dependent — it consults FOUR pre-pass inputs:
        (i) borrow_sources (per sec-1.9)
        (ii) project_alias_sources (per sec-1.9)
        (iii) live-variable set at the ProgramPoint
        (iv) IC-3 ParamContract.uniqueness (per sec-5 IC-3)
    - DP-5 is the upstream sub-predicate composed by rows (a), (b),
      (c), (c-prime) per Annex E §AIMS DP-9 + sec-05.2 DP-9 row
      (c) joint DP-5 refinement
    - DP-9 / IC-3 / DP-5 dependency chain is non-cyclic at the proof-
      obligation level: DP-9 reads IC-3.uniqueness as opaque upstream
      input; sec-06 IC-3 SCC fixpoint computation is structurally
      independent of DP-9 (IC-N derivation rules operate on per-
      instruction TF-N forward outputs + componentwise-max joins + CN
      canonicalization; DP-N predicates NEVER consulted in IC-N
      derivation per Annex E §AIMS)
    - Row (c) safety per agy blind-spot 6 (cured): IC-3.uniqueness = u
      proves the value is NOT shared at function entry; it does NOT
      prove the value has no active LOCAL borrows at the mutation
      point. Row (c) StaticUnique is sound IFF DP-5 ALSO returns true
      locally; when DP-5 returns false the configuration falls through
      to Dynamic (row c-prime)

  Soundness property:
    Forall (s, var, field, point, instruction_kind, ic3_uniqueness).
      cow_mode(s, var, field, point, instruction_kind, ic3_uniqueness)
       = match (s.uniqueness,
                can_mutate_in_place(s, var, field, point,
                                    instruction_kind),
                ic3_uniqueness)
         with
         | (u, true, any) -> StaticUnique -- row (a)
         | (u, false, any) -> StaticShared -- row (b)
         | (ms, true, u) -> StaticUnique -- row (c)
         | (ms, false, u) -> Dynamic -- row (c-prime)
         | (ms, any, non-u) -> Dynamic -- row (d)
         | (s, any, any) -> StaticShared -- row (e)

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Exhaustive enumeration over the (Uniqueness x DP-5-result x
          ic3_uniqueness) product per Appendix C DP-9 + row (c) joint
          refinement.
      (b) Soundness equality on every enumerated row + non-cyclic
          dependency on sec-06 IC-3 (DP-9 reads IC-3.uniqueness as
          opaque upstream input).

    Part (a) — Appendix C DP-9 row partition (6 rows post (c) /
    (c-prime) refinement, exhaustive):

      Row (a): Uniqueness = u AND DP-5 = true -> StaticUnique
        Soundness: RC = 1 + no active overlapping borrow locally ->
        in-place mutation safe with NO runtime check. DP-5 already
        proved the local borrow-safety obligation.

      Row (b): Uniqueness = u AND DP-5 = false -> StaticShared
        Soundness: RC = 1 (IsShared on Unique always returns false)
        but active overlapping borrow forbids in-place mutation. A
        runtime IsShared check would return false and incorrectly
        route to the in-place arm; therefore the runtime check is
        UNSOUND with active borrows. Static copy is the only correct
        discharge.

      Row (c): Uniqueness = ms AND DP-5 = true AND
                IC-3.uniqueness = u -> StaticUnique
        Soundness: caller proved RC == 1 (past guarantee from
        interprocedural contract per Annex E §AIMS IC-3) AND
        local borrow-safety holds (DP-5 = true). Both checks compose:
        IC-3 eliminates the inter-procedural sharing risk; DP-5
        eliminates the intra-procedural alias-overlap risk. Per sec-4
        DP-9 safety clauses (a) callee-local Let Var aliases
        transparent (no inc; Project borrows caught by DP-5) +
        (b) caller-retained alias caught by IC-3 fixpoint convergence
        to ms, NOT u.

      Row (c-prime): Uniqueness = ms AND DP-5 = false AND
                 IC-3.uniqueness = u -> Dynamic
        Soundness: IC-3 proves not shared at entry but DP-5 reveals
        local borrow blocks in-place; the joint check refinement (per
        agy blind-spot 6 cure + sec-05.2 success criterion) forces
        fall-through to Dynamic. The Dynamic runtime IsShared check is
        sound here because IC-3.uniqueness = u combined with backward
        analysis preserving ms at the local point means the local
        refcount may have grown via caller-retained aliases; the
        runtime check resolves the dynamic case.

      Row (d): Uniqueness = ms AND IC-3.uniqueness != u (or row (c)
                precondition otherwise unmet) -> Dynamic
        Soundness: no interprocedural guarantee + no static local
        guarantee -> runtime IsShared check is required.

      Row (e): Uniqueness = s -> StaticShared
        Soundness: RC > 1 proved statically -> unconditional copy. The
        IC-3 + DP-5 sub-predicate values are non-load-bearing for this
        row.

    Part (b) — Coverage gate:
      Per the verifier section_05::verify_dp9_cow_mode_classification:
        Uniqueness axis: 3 values (u, ms, s).
        DP-5 result axis: 2 (true, false).
        IC-3 uniqueness axis: 3 (u, ms, s).
        Coverage product: 3 x 2 x 3 = 18 enumerated cases per the
        Appendix C row partition + row (c) / (c-prime) joint-DP-5
        refinement.

      Row-by-row classification count (canonical case partition):
        Row (a): u x true x any IC-3 = 1 x 1 x 3 = 3 cases
        Row (b): u x false x any IC-3 = 1 x 1 x 3 = 3 cases
        Row (c): ms x true x u = 1 x 1 x 1 = 1 case
        Row (c-prime): ms x false x u = 1 x 1 x 1 = 1 case
        Row (d): ms x any x (ms, s) = 1 x 2 x 2 = 4 cases
        Row (e): s x any x any IC-3 = 1 x 2 x 3 = 6 cases
        Total: 3 + 3 + 1 + 1 + 4 + 6 = 18 cases — exhaustive.

      Outcome partition (CowMode):
        StaticUnique: 3 (row a) + 1 (row c) = 4
        StaticShared: 3 (row b) + 6 (row e) = 9
        Dynamic: 1 (row c-prime) + 4 (row d) = 5
        Total: 4 + 9 + 5 = 18 — exhaustive.

    Joint-DP-5 refinement witness (row (c) vs row (c-prime)
    discrimination):
      Take s with Uniqueness = ms and IC-3.uniqueness = u.
        If DP-5 = true: cow_mode = StaticUnique (row c).
        If DP-5 = false: cow_mode = Dynamic (row c-prime).
      Two-case split is the closure of the agy blind-spot 6 gap: IC-3
      alone could not prove local borrow safety; row (c) discharges
      ONLY when DP-5 also holds locally.

    Negative-direction witness — Unique + DP-5 false counterexample:
      Consider s with Uniqueness = u; DP-5 returns false because a
      live overlapping borrow exists. Per the predicate row (b) ->
      cow_mode = StaticShared. Sound: runtime IsShared on Unique
      would always return false; the in-place arm would corrupt the
      borrowed view; static copy is the only correct discharge.

    Negative-direction witness — MaybeShared + IC-3.uniqueness = u +
    DP-5 false:
      Consider s with Uniqueness = ms, IC-3.uniqueness = u, DP-5 =
      false. Per the predicate row (c-prime) -> cow_mode = Dynamic.
      Sound: IC-3 proves not-shared at entry but the local DP-5 check
      forces fall-through; the Dynamic runtime IsShared check
      resolves the case at runtime — closure of the agy blind-spot 6
      gap.

    Negative-direction witness — Shared + DP-5 + IC-3 irrelevant:
      Consider s with Uniqueness = s, any DP-5 value, any IC-3
      uniqueness. Per the predicate row (e) -> cow_mode = StaticShared.
      Sound: RC > 1 proven statically; the DP-5 and IC-3 sub-predicate
      values are non-load-bearing for this row.

    cow_mode classification declaration:
      rows: a, b, c, c-prime, d, e
      row_c_joint_dp5_refinement: required
      upstream_inputs: borrow_sources, project_alias_sources,
                       live_variable_set, ic3_param_contract_uniqueness
      cycle_break: per the DP-9 / IC-3 cycle-break decision
                   (DP-9 reads IC-3.uniqueness as opaque; sec-06 IC-3
                   SCC fixpoint is structurally independent of DP-9)

    Live-variable / borrow_sources / project_alias_sources / IC-3
    contract typed pre-pass dependency: REQUIRED for DP-9 (DP-9
    composes DP-5 typed pre-pass dependency for rows (a), (b), (c),
    (c-prime); DP-9 additionally consumes IC-3.uniqueness as opaque
    upstream input per Annex E §AIMS DP-9 +
    the proof-checker design Engine-per-Category-Inventory
    DP-row line 99). The verifier constructs synthetic (DP-5-result,
    IC-3.uniqueness) fixtures per row of the truth table; the fixture
    suite is encoded in section_05::verify_dp9_cow_mode_classification.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix C 6-row enumeration over
        (Uniqueness x DP-5-result x IC-3.uniqueness) product with the
        row (c) / (c-prime) joint-DP-5 refinement axis per
        section_05::verify_dp9_cow_mode_classification; the verifier
        checks the soundness equality cow_mode-vs-row-partition on
        every enumerated case and emits Fail on any divergence)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_05 case_analysis engine discharges DP-9 via 18-case enumeration over (Uniqueness x DP-5-result x IC-3.uniqueness) covering Appendix C 6-row classification (rows a, b, c, c-prime, d, e) including the row (c) joint-DP-5 refinement per Annex E §AIMS DP-9 + sec-05.2 success criterion
